#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277979 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71da663-e7a4-5781-973c-5dc7e4deb83f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points of Intersection of a Horizontal Line and a Tangent Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64665c65-a217-51f5-8b50-4ce3d6c2bc6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277981} {:answer/id #uuid "49bce2c0-7111-5786-8d41-c1887b6cb48d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277982} {:answer/id #uuid "e69e16d0-fee5-54d3-a02b-cc2ee311af9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8\\pi }{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277983} {:answer/id #uuid "fc9eb9a0-3d07-5668-ac3e-e9d02100b319" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277984} {:answer/id #uuid "6d57f986-db13-514b-ab92-c979718aa86d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d57f986-db13-514b-ab92-c979718aa86d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277985} :answer-field/id #uuid "47929783-18a2-5a5a-918b-3a7c899616ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277980}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "40f7d319-bfe9-5828-b013-a9a68e7eb115" :question/math-academy-id "q-121542" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977868/assets/56726fc8331106df9b20aed561a2ed3b93fe12d90da85a8d1b92e610b19033f7.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=\\sqrt{3}.$ Find the $x$-coordinate of the point $B.$\n\n$$\n\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two equations gives: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis value lies outside $-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<x<-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ To get a value that's inside the required domain, we add $-\\pi $  to the principal value. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=-\\pi +x=-\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3}=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinate of $B$ is $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71da663-e7a4-5781-973c-5dc7e4deb83f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points of Intersection of a Horizontal Line and a Tangent Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94f8b14f-8fe0-527f-b3be-dfaee31315b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277988} {:answer/id #uuid "bfdf1082-baca-55f0-b3c8-148cd49f2361" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfdf1082-baca-55f0-b3c8-148cd49f2361" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277989} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e829784-352e-546b-b589-dc5d8deeeb5f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277987}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d180bdf2-fe1c-5547-a6bb-3dbae8427806" :question/math-academy-id "q-274852" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977868/assets/047f02622fc176fee8c6cb0e81a0434ee208648dca14102b1d96e37b901d51f2.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=1.$\n\nThe **exact** value of the $x$-coordinate of the point $A$ is \n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two equations gives:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis value lies outside $-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<x<-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ To get a value that's inside the required domain, we add $-\\pi $ to the principal value. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =x+(-\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\pi  \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinate of $A$ is $-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277990 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c7ab50-5a8b-5bcd-8483-cec8bf6bd3ce" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent with Non-Special Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95d4ea44-d1c7-5a57-8c4b-c552f9b48ea9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95d4ea44-d1c7-5a57-8c4b-c552f9b48ea9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277992} :answer-field/id #uuid "86ac4f73-8253-5b38-8431-20e467ca1ad5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277991} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32b9adcf-ccbb-577c-b00a-654888926547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "189" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32b9adcf-ccbb-577c-b00a-654888926547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "189" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277994} :answer-field/id #uuid "4104241c-1ccd-5359-ad5b-f7628f4def96" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277993}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "64dbab80-af43-59e4-8d97-d949c8f2ff4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-321622" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in degrees** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{1}{6}$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ Round your answers to **the nearest integer**.\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arctan\\,(\\frac{1}{6})=9.4623{…}^{∘}≈{9}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${9}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={9}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+9.4623{…}^{∘}≈{189}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions are $x={9}^{∘}$ and $x={189}^{∘}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277995 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c7ab50-5a8b-5bcd-8483-cec8bf6bd3ce" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent with Non-Special Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dbe7c01-e369-57d3-b4d3-2aa7b3f424bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277997} {:answer/id #uuid "4849510a-f2db-5905-a715-d49ffc472fc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277998} {:answer/id #uuid "85239dd0-8edd-577c-be8d-3ad4a247bfda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277999} {:answer/id #uuid "daa3bbb7-7a62-5f02-a7c0-0b9268fa6df3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278000} {:answer/id #uuid "561aca6a-b656-5ddc-bdc5-5fb329ac7b18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85239dd0-8edd-577c-be8d-3ad4a247bfda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277999} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b4d9ab4-51c5-5dc6-a7af-e60ea74a4d13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277996}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "63edf08b-7802-5b9f-940f-83ad72d838db" :question/math-academy-id "q-72824" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-8$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to one decimal place?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-8)=-1.446\\,4…≈-1.446\\,4.\n$$\n\nSince $-1.446\\,4$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\pi -1.446\\,4≈1.695\\,2, \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2\\pi -1.446\\,4≈4.836\\,8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈1.695\\,2\\cdot 4.836\\,8≈8.2\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278002 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebf8592e-1a43-5d65-af3c-9becd79ae8b9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30e715b7-82d3-5959-9197-8f18a36ad843" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278004} {:answer/id #uuid "20167ebf-c31f-5ccd-8d2c-3682f252954e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278005} {:answer/id #uuid "97e341fc-f53d-5bfc-bd3a-23ade7428705" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278006} {:answer/id #uuid "a3464676-c759-5e6c-b2fa-887a7e2a9bac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278007} {:answer/id #uuid "7cec39a0-69f0-524e-830a-c99d3badc0ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3464676-c759-5e6c-b2fa-887a7e2a9bac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278007} :answer-field/id #uuid "176b0e2e-8b22-54dd-afac-d234aba9e08f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "417331c2-762c-5bf7-9ba6-a204c035e2e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-8720" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-5\\sqrt{3}=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-5\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =5\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=-\\pi +{x}_{1}=-\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3}=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{2\\pi }{3})=-\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{9}.\n$$"}]}
